  "review": {
    "summary": "The remaining documentation MINOR for WP-07 is fixed in docs/launch/local-database-development.md (snapshot sha256:081855c5…612b66). The final paragraph now says that when `DATABASE_URL` is injected, tests reuse it, including the allowed local dev DB. It also says that before switching from development to testing, a dedicated disposable test URL must be injected into the session, and the interactive dev database must not be reused. That makes clear that the shared URL resolver used by pretest and Vitest will not move tests off the dev DB on its own. Users need to take an explicit step first. The doc already tells users to check the target with `npm run db:check` and to use a disposable DB for baselines, which supports this. The doc still keeps the other caveats: the unit-only command is not full acceptance, the concurrency and contract suites must be run separately, and no single step replaces CI or WP acceptance. I found no new substantive defects in this document. Per scope, I reviewed only this document; product code and tests (snapshot sha256:2aa7e3fb…aa06) were not re-reviewed. No findings here does not certify that tests or the release pass.",
